{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/866829-story-thread","id":866829,"title":"Story Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-17T07:57:38-07:00","id":866829,"title":"Story Thread","content":"Quite simply, this is a thread for the sharing of you Beast stories, whether of play or simply stories that you've written. Anyone is welcome to post.<br /> <br /> <b><u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Challenge</span></u></b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">The creature named Anya sat on the outcropping of rock over the dark lake and waited for the Hero to arrive.<br /> <br /> The breeze wafted in over the still water between the blue mountains on either side. It was peaceful. It was such a pity that she\u2019d have to fight on such a lovely evening.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s left the Serpent hungry for too long, being paranoid about one of <i>his </i>kind finding her. It was ironic that it was her very caution that brought him. A Hero. Anya snorted at the thought. Such a ridiculous name. But then again, to the humans (those who didn\u2019t get in his way at least), he must have seemed to be a hero. The strapping twenty-something lad from out of town who turned up investigating the reports of disappearances on the lake with a pack on his back and a smile for all the girls. It wasn\u2019t like she took them forever. Not even a day, mostly.<br /> <br /> Besides, if she didn\u2019t scare them away from going up that end of the lake, there would be no telling what the thing made out of wings and eyes and</span><span style=\"font-size:14px\">gears</span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> in the cave would do to them. She\u2019d seen what it had done to the man with the silver eyes who tried to sneak in that one time. His eyes were plucked out, his skin torn to reveal the crystal clockworks underneath. A week later, she\u2019d seen him come out of that cave again. Only this time, it wasn\u2019t the same man. It looked the same, it had the same face, but there was something else behind the eyes, something worse than a creature made of silver and crystal gears.<br /> <br /> And for keeping them away from that <i>thing</i> while she tried to find a way to get rid of it, they\u2019d pointed the Hero in her direction and <i>paid</i> him to get rid of her, like she was some kind of animal. So she\u2019d made sure that he faced her at a time and place that worked in her favour.<br /> <br /> Heroes never could resist a challenge, after all.<br /> <br /> She laughed hollowly, wheezing the sound up a throat unused to air. It was so like humans to try to destroy the very thing that protected them.<br /> <br /> The sound of booted footsteps behind her jolted her from her thoughts. Without turning, she called out to him down the outcrop.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo. You came then.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course I came!\u201d he declared in what he probably thought sounded like a heroic voice, \u201cHow could I ignore the cries of the oppressed down in the village!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat oppressed? I keep to my end of the lake, they should keep to theirs. I\u2019ve been here longer they have after all. Why shouldn\u2019t I keep my land?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSpeak no more lies, monster!\u201d he yelled, spittle flying from his lips. He moved up the outcrop. \u201cLet us battle here for the fate of this land!\u201d<br /> <br /> Anya laughed, high and wild, \u201cWhere did you get that spiel? A fantasy novel?\u201d She stopped laughing and looked him in the eye. \u201cYou really are a fool aren\u2019t you. You accepted a challenge to battle the monster of the on the shores of the lake itself. How stupid are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> His face went red with fury. He reached for the gun at his side. She stepped forward, knocked it out of his hand and held his arms still with impossible strength. \u201cI\u2019m sorry it had to come to this\u201d she whispered, before hurling him into the lake and leaping after him.<br /> <br /> As she fell, she called the Serpent of the Lake to her, into her. She shed her human form like a used skin, scales bursting from her flesh. Even as her spine lengthened and her limbs shrank, she wrapped around him, bearing him down into the depths until his lungs burst and water rushed in to take the place of air.<br /> <br /> And then she rested because after all, what does the monster do when it kills the hero?<br /> <br /> And if she wept for a life wasted, only the fishes of the lake knew of her tears.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}